-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- the plan of a #jit
-- jit-plan g rules: for checked definition g, (verdict , (ok , (path , (code , bytes)))):
--   verdict: fo when the program is compilable (lib/machine.cub's fragment, then x-check);
--   ok: the checker's conversion of g's value with the meaning of the specialized code (true when
--       the code means g; with no rule applied this is the whole check);
--   path: the code of the path from g's code to the specialized one (refl when no rule applied),
--       which the #jit directive gives to the checker when rules were applied;
--   code: the specialized code; bytes: the blob.
x-arity-is : Defs → Word → Word → Bool
x-arity-is defs g n = case x-arity defs g return (λ _ → Bool) of
  some k → %weq k n
  none → false
